    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Website:</strong> Tej Photography</p>
    <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 7 June 2026</p>

    <div class="note">
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Tej Photography collects, uses, stores, and protects user information when visitors use our photography portfolio, client gallery, print purchase, subscription, payment proof upload, referral, and contact services.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect the following information when you use this website:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name, email address, phone number, and message submitted through contact forms.</li>
      <li>Client login details such as email, password, membership level, gallery access, VIP access status, and expiry date.</li>
      <li>Payment-related details such as UPI ID, transaction ID, payment screenshot/proof, payment status, cart details, selected print size, and subscription plan.</li>
      <li>Referral codes, coupon usage, discount details, and earned coupon information.</li>
      <li>Uploaded photos/videos or client gallery data added by the website owner/admin.</li>
      <li>Basic browser/device information, if analytics or technical logs are added later.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>Your information may be used to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide access to private client galleries.</li>
      <li>Manage subscriptions, VIP access, discounts, referrals, and memberships.</li>
      <li>Review and approve or reject payment proof manually.</li>
      <li>Process print purchase requests and client inquiries.</li>
      <li>Contact you regarding your order, gallery, subscription, or support request.</li>
      <li>Improve website features, security, and user experience.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Payment Information</h2>
    <p>Tej Photography may use QR code/UPI payment for demo or manual payment confirmation. We do not automatically unlock paid access until the owner/admin approves the payment. Users may be asked to upload transaction ID and payment screenshot as proof.</p>
    <p>This website does not collect card numbers, bank passwords, OTPs, or sensitive banking credentials. Never share such details through this website.</p>

    <h2>4. LocalStorage Demo System</h2>
    <p>If the website is running without a backend server, some information may be stored in the browser using localStorage for demo purposes. localStorage data is stored on the user’s device and may not provide full production-level security.</p>
    <p>For a real business website, we recommend using a secure backend, database, server-side authentication, encrypted passwords, HTTPS, and trusted payment gateway integration.</p>

    <h2>5. Password-Protected Galleries</h2>
    <p>Private client galleries are intended only for authorized users with valid email and password access. Users must not share private gallery links, passwords, downloaded content, or client photos/videos without permission.</p>

    <h2>6. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
    <p>This website may use browser storage, cookies, or similar technologies to remember login status, membership access, cart items, coupons, and preferences. If analytics or advertising tools are added later, they may collect additional usage data according to their own policies.</p>

    <h2>7. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. Information may be shared only when necessary to operate the website, process orders, comply with legal requirements, prevent fraud, or protect the rights and safety of Tej Photography and its users.</p>

    <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
    <p>We aim to protect user data using reasonable security practices. However, no website, browser storage, or internet transmission is 100% secure. Users are responsible for keeping their login details confidential.</p>

    <h2>9. User Rights</h2>
    <p>You may contact Tej Photography to request access, correction, or deletion of your personal information, subject to valid business, legal, or security requirements.</p>

    <h2>10. Children’s Privacy</h2>
    <p>This website is not intended for children under 13 years of age. If a child’s information is submitted without parental permission, please contact us for removal.</p>

    <h2>11. Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>The website may contain social media links or external links. Tej Photography is not responsible for the privacy practices, content, or security of third-party websites.</p>

    <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updated versions will be posted on this page with a revised “Last Updated” date.</p>

